<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manjakamiadana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manjakamiadana was the queen's palace, the largest building of the Rova, the royal compound of the Merina rulers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Antananarivo</a>. Built in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranavalona-i">Ranavalona I</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-laborde">Jean Laborde</a> around 1840, it was encased in stone between 1867 and 1873 to designs by the missionary James Cameron. Gutted by fire in 1995, it has since been restored.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manjakamiadana.jpg" alt="Manjakamiadana" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hery Zo Rakotondramanana · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reconstructed_Rova_Antananarivo_Madagascar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
